<jnt = 'http://www.jahia.org/jahia/nt/1.0'>
<jmix = 'http://www.jahia.org/jahia/mix/1.0'>

[jnt:statuspageIoWidget] > jnt:content, jmix:droppableContent
 // pageId value constraint (write-side XSS hardening, SUPPORT-646): JCR rejects any value that is
 // not a safe DNS-subdomain label (a-z, 0-9, hyphen; length 1-63) at setValue/save time. This is a
 // deliberate defense-in-depth layer so the render-path allowlist in statuspageIoWidget.jsp is no
 // longer the SOLE guard against stored XSS. The regex is kept IDENTICAL to that JSP allowlist
 // ([a-z0-9-], 1-63 chars) so write-path and render-path agree exactly for this per-node property.
 // NOTE (D7 residual): the GLOBAL OSGi-config path uses a stricter DNS regex
 // (^[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?$, no leading/trailing hyphen) and the JS util is looser
 // (allows uppercase). Fully unifying all four validators via one shared constant is not achievable
 // across CND/Java/JSP/JS; that convergence is left as a maintainer follow-up.
 - pageId (string) mandatory < '[a-z0-9-]{1,63}'